# Scheduled-only policy/VLA-private Global -> Pipeline binding protocol.
# Global supplies a UUID4 session_id and its positive logical_generation.
# binding_id (UUID4) and positive binding_incarnation identify this binding;
# expected_boot_id (UUID4) fences the Pipeline process. None may be omitted.
# operation_id is the UUID4 of this downstream operation and is echoed back.
# Idempotency key: session_id, within this Pipeline's retained ledger.
# Duplicates preserve all identity fields, including operation_id; changing
# them conflicts. Duplicates wait for or replay the original result.
# NOT_STARTED permits retry; UNKNOWN requires fenced cleanup, never blind retry.
# Open cancellation is rejected. Caller timeout does not stop reset/device work;
# a late accepted Open still requires identity-fenced Close cleanup.
string<=36 session_id
uint64 logical_generation
string<=36 binding_id
uint64 binding_incarnation
string<=36 operation_id
string<=36 expected_boot_id
# Required positive absolute UTC Unix time, never ROS/simulation/monotonic time.
# Global resolves the public default; zero is invalid on this private action.
# Duplicate Open cannot extend the original operation's deadline.
builtin_interfaces/Time deadline
---
bool success
string<=36 session_id
uint64 logical_generation
string<=36 binding_id
uint64 binding_incarnation
string<=36 operation_id
string<=36 boot_id
string<=63 pipeline_id
# Positive on successful Open; zero may appear on failure before admission.
uint64 pipeline_generation
string<=64 deployment_fingerprint
string<=64 runtime_policy_fingerprint
# Pipeline ROS-clock expiry projected from its monotonic lease; zero on failure.
builtin_interfaces/Time lease_expires_at
ibrobot_msgs/InferenceOutcome outcome
ibrobot_msgs/ScheduledInferenceError error
---
string<=128 status
